{"id":"taopad-2024","slug":"taopad-2024","sub":null,"name":"TaoPad","date":"2024-02-14","one_liner":"TaoPad's own operator tx to pull the token's 29.2 ETH tax balance ran out of gas; Yoink replayed its calls 4 min later (net 26.32 ETH) and returned it all the next day after the team wrote to it.","bot":"Yoink","race_type":"post-failure-replay","narrative":"The counterparty is not a hacker: it is the TaoPad project's own operator wallet taopad.eth (0x98915686..., deployer and operator of the TPAD token), extracting the ETH that the TPAD token contract had accumulated from taxes (about 29.18 ETH) by using a bug in the token's public distribute(minOut) (a permissionless swap of the whole ETH balance with a caller-chosen minimum-out through the operator-set Uniswap V3 fee tier), the same weakness that had been exploited by a third party weeks earlier (per TaoPad's own messages; not independently identified here). The operator deployed a helper contract (block 19226396), set poolFee to 100 (19226402) and sent execute() with 1 ETH (public mempool first seen 2024-02-14T13:23:12.276Z, block 19226482 index 0, 13:23:23Z). That tx REVERTED out of gas inside its second swap (gas limit 29,792,302). Yoink's tx 0x5853b7a0... (block 19226503, index 0, 13:27:35Z; not in the mempool archive, private flow) repeats the operator's victim-protocol call sequence (6 core calls: createPool, pool initialize and distribute(0) byte-identical after normalising the two contracts; the two swaps and the liquidity mint identical except the deadline and one amount-bound word), with a 30,000,000 gas limit, finishes the extraction and sells: 29.5056 ETH in, 1.0 ETH working capital out, 1.3968 ETH to the coinbase, 0.7847 ETH gas, 26.3242 ETH net. It landed 21 blocks (252 s after the failure's block time, 263 s after the operator's tx was first seen) AFTER the operator's tx had already failed on chain; no tx of the operator was pending in between (the operator's next tx is setPoolFee(0) at block 19226577, after Yoink), and nobody else called distribute() in blocks 19226300-19226700 (trace_filter). So Yoink did not pre-empt anything: it succeeded where the operator's tx had failed (post-failure replay of a non-hacker's tx). TaoPad's message says Yoink 'frontran' them; the chain shows a replay after the operator's own out-of-gas failure. Yoink answered the same evening asking whether it was 'a failed rug attempt', then on 2024-02-15 12:53:35Z sent 26.32 ETH (exact) back to taopad.eth in tx 0xa0346352... ('sent back the entire bot profit'): 26.32 of a 26.324 ETH net (99.98%).","chain":"ethereum","verdict":"related-not-frontrun","t0_ms":1707917255000,"pre_merge":false,"premerge_note":null,"slot":8424436,"block":{"number":19226503,"hash":"0x7cf3efa4607245390a9daa861cf73a682d0dbee1f0a24269b58787486aacb6b6","ts_ms":1707917255000,"ntx":13,"builder":"https://blockbeelder.com \ud83d\udc1d","fee_recipient":"0x7adc0e867ebc337e2d20c44db181c067fa08637b","gas_used":29998043,"base_fee_gwei":26.709476643,"raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_19226503.json","receipts":"raw/rpc/receipts_19226503.json","trace":"raw/rpc/trace_block_19226503.json","slot":null}},"strip":[[0,1,"bot",0.0,1.3968],[1,1,"",1.0,0.0],[2,1,"",48.291,0.0],[3,1,"",23.291,0.0],[4,1,"",15.304,0.0],[5,1,"",14.0,0.0],[6,1,"",13.291,0.0],[7,1,"",12.298,0.0],[8,1,"",7.5,0.0],[9,1,"",7.341,0.0],[10,1,"",5.697,0.0],[11,1,"",5.0,0.0],[12,1,"builder",0.0,0.0]],"txs":[{"i":0,"h":"0x5853b7a0b09f600baf44317ccc311382c9bc5d954b21968ac0ee3cbae3481c3e","from_":"0xfde0d1575ed8e06fbf36256bcdfa1f359281455a","to":"0x6980a47bee930a4584b09ee79ebe46484fbdbdd0","role":"bot","ok":true,"value_eth":0.0,"cb_eth":1.396774,"sel":"0x9846cd9e","gas":29377748,"tip":0.0,"err":null,"label":null,"bundle_like":null,"raw":{"tx":"raw/rpc/block_19226503.json","receipt":"raw/rpc/receipts_19226503.json","trace":"raw/rpc/trace_block_19226503.json"}},{"i":12,"h":"0xd4405f3beee60d05b6e54f7a4356e9e4e98c971751b8003076de03e5fa91107b","from_":"0x7adc0e867ebc337e2d20c44d